  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ASSESSING THE DISTRIBUTION AND STATUS OF THE CRITICALLY ENDANGERED NUBIAN FLAPSHELL TURTLE AND ENHANCING COMMUNITY CAPACITY FOR CONSERVATION IN NORTHERN UGANDA</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">THE PURPOSE OF THIS PROJECT IS TO IMPLEMENT CONSERVATION ACTIVITIES TO PROTECT THIS SPECIES FROM EXPLOITATION FOR CONSUMPTION BY LOCAL FISHERS AND FOR SALE THIS SPECIES WAS SUSPECTED TO BE EXTINCT IN THE WILD, BUT A POPULATION WAS REDISCOVERED ALONG THE WHITE NILE RIVER IN SOUTHERN SUDAN IN 2017, AND AGAIN IN A REMOTE AREA OF NORTHERN UGANDA IN AUGUST 2021. ACTIVITIES INCLUDE: (1) CONDUCTING THREE, 10-DAY FIELD SURVEYS IN NORTHERN UGANDA TO DETERMINE ITS DISTRIBUTION AND POPULATION SIZE (2) CONSULTING WITH STAKEHOLDERS TO DETERMINE BEST PRACTICES FOR CONDUCTING AN AWARENESS CAMPAIGN WITH LOCAL COMMUNITIES (3) DEVELOPING OUTREACH MATERIALS IN COLLABORATION WITH GOVERNMENT AGENCIES AND (4) CONDUCTING AWARENESS CAMPAIGNS AND MEETINGS WITH LOCAL COMMUNITY LEADERS AND CITIZENS (INCLUDING YOUTH) TO ASSIST WITH ONGOING COMMUNITY OUTREACH AND AWARENESS FOR PROTECTION OF THIS SPECIES.</narrative>
  </description>
